{"The offset clamping allows offset === user_count, which will fetch an empty page. After member additions/deletions, this can cause pagination desynchronization. Should clamp to Math.max(this.get(\"user_count\") - this.get(\"limit\"), 0) as the upper bound": 0.5650634169578552, "The totalPages formula incorrectly calculates an extra page when user_count is an exact multiple of limit (e.g., 100 users with limit 50 returns 3 pages instead of 2). Should use Math.ceil(this.get(\"user_count\") / this.get(\"limit\")) instead": 0.940767228603363, "Function returns undefined instead of a promise when the name is empty, which is a contract change from the previous Ember.RSVP.resolve([]). Callers expecting promise chaining may break": 0.900894045829773, "The username parsing doesn't normalize or trim whitespace. Should use usernames.split(\",\").map(&:strip).reject(&:blank?).uniq to handle input variations consistently": 0.6293880343437195, "The limit parameter is not clamped to a safe maximum, allowing potential abuse or performance degradation from excessively large limit values. Should clamp to a maximum like 200": 0.7185937762260437, "The response format changed from a simple serialized array to an object with members and meta properties, which is a breaking API change that could impact existing consumers (plugins, mobile apps, or other clients)": 0.8404364585876465}